Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:09:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix: verify migration hashes, real UTC recovery points
 and exact rerun no-op in the preview DB guard

Gaps in the guard added in 2ea4b4f, each reproduced against it:
- recovery_point only matched a timestamp prefix: '2026-02-30T10:00'
  passed. Now a strict UTC instant with Z, a real calendar date/time and
  not in the future. It is recorded as OWNER_ATTESTED (providerVerified:
  false), never as a verified backup; pre also fails if any TIMESTAMP
  createdAt/updatedAt row is newer than the attested point.
- the journal check compared created_at only: a tampered
  __drizzle_migrations hash passed. Now each applied row must match the
  Drizzle migrator format exactly (hash = sha256 of drizzle/<tag>.sql,
  created_at = journal 'when'); verified against rows written by
  drizzle-kit migrate (pnpm db:push).
- the 'rerun is a no-op' step re-ran the post check (completeness and
  minimum row counts). A new 'rerun' mode now requires journal rows,
  tables, columns, indexes, constraints and row counts to equal the
  post snapshot exactly.

Regression: tests/preview-migration-guard.test.mjs (24: malformed and
future dates, wrong hash/created_at, out-of-order and extra journal
rows, snapshot diffs, workflow wiring) and
tests/preview-migration-guard.mysql.test.mjs (6, real MySQL 8 with the
Drizzle migrator: full guarded sequence, rows newer than the recovery
point, tampered hash, missing/extra journal rows, schema/journal/data
change during the rerun, row loss, wrong database name).

